<title>AUSTRALIA: Australia labour court chief O'Connor quits.</title>
<headline>Australia labour court chief O'Connor quits.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Career lawyer Deidre O'Connor on Wednesday formally resigned as president of the Australian Industrial Relations Commission, Workplace Relations Minister Peter Reith said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>O'Connor, 56, who has held the position since 1994 would be replaced in due course, Reith said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Canberra Bureau 61-6 273-2730</p>
